{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.Reason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Cover Letter, December 2024], [Design and Access Statement, December 2024], [Brentford Fountain Heritage Impact Assessment, December 2024], [Brentford Fountain - Condition Survey and Methodology for Dismantle, December 2024], Existing Site Plan 1-1250 - 13366-BNY-A-DR-SA-00-001], [Title Ownership Boundary - 13366-BNY-A-DR-SA-00-002], [Planning Boundary - 13366-BNY-A-DR-SA-00-003], Received: 23/12/2024].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - A scheme describing the method of demolition, removal, storage, and reinstatement of the monument shall be submitted to and agreed by the local planning authority prior to development taking place and these works shall be carried out as approved. \r\nReason: To ensure the satisfactory treatment of the historic fabric of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - A Level 2 Record in accordance with Historic England's 'Understanding Historic Buildings - A Guide to Good Recording Practice' (May 2016) will be submitted to the local planning authority and relevant authorities within six months of the dismantling works taking place. The Level 2 Recording will be carried out in accordance with the approved Written Scheme of Investigation set out within the Condition Survey and Methodology for Dismantle prepared by PAYE.\r\nReason: To ensure the satisfactory recording of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - A scheme of investigation to assess the nature of the fixings within the monument shall be submitted to and agreed by the local planning authority prior to development taking place and carried out as approved, prior to determining the method of dismantling of the structure. \r\nReason: To ensure the method of dismantling is appropriate to the historic fabric of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - In respect of the removal of the fountain, the local planning authority shall be given 14 days' notice of the intention to carry out the works and the Conservation Officer shall be allowed access to the fountain to enable him to take photographs of the site and the fountain before it is removed in continuance of the work for which consent has been given. \r\nReason: The fountain's location and context have the potential to contribute towards historic significance.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Prior to the occupation of the development, a Conservation Management and Action Plan (CMAP), which sets out the ongoing actions necessary to sustain the significance of the during heritage asset, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, in conjunction with Historic England.\r\nIn particular, the CMAP shall identify and include: \r\ni.\tWho will be responsible for the long-term management; \r\nii.\tThe necessary repair and maintenance tasks and the frequency with which they will be undertaken; \r\niii.\tAn ongoing maintenance schedule; \r\niv.\tEnhancement of the presentation of the site to improve public understanding and enjoyment;\r\nv.\tHow future maintenance will be funded in the long term; \r\nvi.\tRoutine building maintenance schedule, to include: \r\na.\tClearing leaves, snow, controlling plant growth, removal of bird soiling;\r\nb.\tRemoval of graffiti; \r\nc.\tInspection and clearing of drainage; \r\nd.\tRepairs to masonry and external finishes; \r\ne.\tMaintenance of hard and soft landscaping; \r\nf.\tMaintenance of any interpretative panels and presentation schemes.\r\nThe CMAP shall set out the arrangements and timescale for a periodic review of the contents of the plan and the implementation of the action it recommends. \r\nReason: To ensure the satisfactory preservation of the listed building.\r\n"
  ],
